    "hoise": {
      "word": "HOISE",
      "definitions": [
        {
          "text": "To hoist. [Obs.] They . . . hoised up the mainsail to the wind. Acts xxvii. 40.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        }
      ],
      "relatedWords": []
    },
    "hoist": {
      "word": "HOIST",
      "definitions": [
        {
          "text": "To raise; to lift; to elevate; esp., to raise or lift to a desired elevation, by means of tackle, as a sail, a flag, a heavy package or weight. They land my goods, and hoist my flying sails. Pope. Hoisting him into his father's throne. South. Hoisting engine, a steam engine for operating a hoist.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        },
        {
          "text": "That by which anything is hoisted; the apparatus for lifting goods.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "The act of hoisting; a lift. [Collog.]",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "(fly, or horizontal length when flying from a staff. (b) The height of a fore-and-aft sail next the mast or stay. Totten. Hoist bridge, a drawbridge that is lifted instead of being swung or drawn aside.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "Hoisted. [Obs.] 'Tis the sport to have the enginer Hoist with his own petar. Shak.",
          "partOfSpeech": ""
        }
      ],
